---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getCanonicalUrl } from '../utils/seo';

const canonicalUrl = getCanonicalUrl('/editorial-standards');
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Standards & Verification Policy — LifeMode"
  description="LifeMode editorial guidelines, verification protocols, sourcing standards, factual review process, and affiliate transparency."
  canonicalUrl={canonicalUrl}
>
  <div class="page-shell container-prose" style="padding-top: var(--space-8); padding-bottom: var(--space-20);">
    <header style="margin-bottom: var(--space-8);">
      <span class="badge" style="background-color: rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.1); color: var(--color-primary-accent); border: 1px solid rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.2); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem; border-radius: var(--radius-full); margin-bottom: var(--space-3); display: inline-block;">
        Journalism &amp; Ethics
      </span>
      <h1 class="page-title" style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem); font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-text-primary); margin-bottom: var(--space-3);">
        Editorial Standards &amp; Fact-Checking Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="page-lead" style="font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">
        How LifeMode researches, verifies, structures, and maintains practical guidance, recipes, and decision tools.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>1. Purpose &amp; Editorial Mission</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>LifeMode</strong> exists to provide real, actionable, and scientifically sound solutions to daily household challenges and culinary pursuits. We believe every piece of published content must be genuinely useful to a human reader—even if search engines disappeared tomorrow.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Core Sourcing &amp; Research Protocol</h2>
      <p>
        We do not rely on unverified blog posts or recycled internet folklore. Every guide and recipe is anchored in verified primary references:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>University Agricultural Extension Services:</strong> USDA, FDA, state cooperative extension offices, and food safety research centers.</li>
        <li><strong>Material Science &amp; Textile Standards:</strong> ASTM international testing protocols, textile care standards, and manufacturer maintenance specifications.</li>
        <li><strong>Culinary Foundations &amp; Kitchen Science:</strong> Food chemistry, fermentation science, and professional culinary technique.</li>
        <li><strong>Peer-Reviewed Research:</strong> Environmental health, building science, and indoor air quality standards.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. The Fact-Checking Process</h2>
      <p>
        Before any guide is published:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Technical Verification:</strong> Step-by-step procedures are verified against chemical and material safety rules (e.g., pH compatibility for surfaces, thermal shock prevention for cookware).</li>
        <li><strong>Risk &amp; Hazard Screening:</strong> Explicit safety warnings and common mistakes are highlighted to protect user property and personal safety.</li>
        <li><strong>Review &amp; Maintenance:</strong> Content is periodically audited to reflect newer safety standards and improved methodologies.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>4. Editorial Independence &amp; Commercial Transparency</h2>
      <p>
        LifeMode maintains strict editorial independence. If affiliate links or sponsor relationships are present, they are clearly disclosed. Recommendations are formulated entirely on functional merit, durability, safety, and practical efficacy.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Corrections &amp; Reader Inquiries</h2>
      <p>
        If you spot a factual error, outdated specification, or safety concern in any of our guides or tools, please notify our editorial desk immediately:
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Editorial Desk:</strong> <a href="mailto:editorial@lifemode.life">editorial@lifemode.life</a><br />
        <strong>General Inquiries:</strong> <a href="mailto:contact@lifemode.life">contact@lifemode.life</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
